1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,118
You are on a space mission, feeling more tired than

2
00:00:03,118 --> 00:00:03,485
usual.

3
00:00:03,485 --> 00:00:08,177
You have some measurements, limited equipment, and communication with Earth

4
00:00:08,177 --> 00:00:09,428
that may be delayed.

5
00:00:09,428 --> 00:00:11,491
What information should you review?

6
00:00:11,491 --> 00:00:12,906
What can you do now?

7
00:00:12,906 --> 00:00:16,760
We are Astra Vitae, from Argentina, and we developed Orbita

8
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:18,328
to support that journey.

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,890
Orbita connects health indicators, physical assessments, and habitat conditions.

10
00:00:32,890 --> 00:00:36,794
Each measurement retains its origin, method, and date.

11
00:00:36,794 --> 00:00:40,936
This helps distinguish an earlier assessment from a recent measurement.

12
00:00:40,936 --> 00:00:44,859
When information is missing, the gap remains visible: a day

13
00:00:44,859 --> 00:00:47,518
without measurements never becomes zero.

14
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,059
Let's follow an example using fictional data.

15
00:00:55,059 --> 00:00:57,777
We report fatigue and open an episode.

16
00:00:57,777 --> 00:01:01,055
The application brings together what we know and what is

17
00:01:01,055 --> 00:01:03,338
missing before presenting a suggestion.

18
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,531
Procedures check preparation and the equipment available for the mission.

19
00:01:13,531 --> 00:01:16,032
The rule in this demonstration is fictional.

20
00:01:16,032 --> 00:01:20,279
Real clinical guidance requires reviewed content with a source and

21
00:01:20,279 --> 00:01:20,793
version.

22
00:01:20,793 --> 00:01:24,924
Orbita does not diagnose conditions or prescribe treatments.

23
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:32,063
After an action, we need to know what happened.

24
00:01:32,063 --> 00:01:35,562
That is why completing a task and recording its result

25
00:01:35,562 --> 00:01:36,793
are separate steps.

26
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,403
The episode can produce a summary of what was observed,

27
00:01:48,403 --> 00:01:51,187
what was measured, and what is still missing.

28
00:01:51,187 --> 00:01:53,802
Sharing requires an explicit decision.

29
00:01:53,802 --> 00:01:57,983
The ground panel demonstrates that exchange through a clearly labeled

30
00:01:57,983 --> 00:01:59,013
local simulation.

31
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:09,107
We built eleven connected views using JavaScript, SVG charts, and

32
00:02:09,107 --> 00:02:10,365
browser storage.

33
00:02:10,365 --> 00:02:14,377
The main application runs locally and can be delivered as

34
00:02:14,377 --> 00:02:15,715
a single HTML file.

35
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,356
NASA research informed the design.

36
00:02:20,356 --> 00:02:24,559
Research cases are kept separate from personal records and retain

37
00:02:24,559 --> 00:02:25,658
their provenance.

38
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:35,379
Our contribution connects information, available resources, and follow-up.

39
00:02:35,379 --> 00:02:39,038
User studies and clinical validation remain pending.

40
00:02:39,038 --> 00:02:39,713
Orbita.

41
00:02:39,713 --> 00:02:41,438
Your health, on board.
